// Test: bugfixes/list_namespace_internal_helper_not_callable
// Grammar: namespace_function_call
// Semantic: FUNC001 — the compiler's own list helpers (`list.allocate`,
//   `list.removeAt`, ...) are not part of the `list.` namespace
//   (stdlib-reference.md §5) and cannot be called from a program
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   FUNC001
//   Function 'list.allocate' not found
//   The `list.` namespace has only `list.concat`, `list.range`, `list.fill` and `list.join`
//
// Regression: `list.allocate(n)` compiled and returned a raw list pointer
// typed as `integer` (developer decision 0.33.184).

start:
	integer raw = list.allocate(4)
	print(raw)
